      "problem": "Calculate $\\Gamma \\left( \\dfrac{5}{2} \\right).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the gamma function at multiples of one-half, we use the following recursive formula:\n\n$$\n\\Gamma(z+1) = z \\Gamma(z), \\qquad \\Gamma \\left( \\dfrac{1}{2} \\right) = \\sqrt{\\pi}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ(\\frac{5}{2}) & =\\frac{3}{2}Γ(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}Γ(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\sqrt{\\pi }\\end{aligned}\n$$",
